        "overview": "Investigated directly against the codebase (file:line citations throughout) rather than assumed. Two things turned out to both be true at once: client-side execution is genuinely more built than expected, and the one piece n8n's whole value proposition depends on — running when nobody has it open — doesn't exist at all yet.",
        "keyQuestions": "Does Twilite's script/task machinery suffice to run a workflow (the contested assumption on the n8n idea graph)? Is 'n8n-style' realistic as modeled-and-executable, or does it have to stay modeled-only until server-side execution exists?",
