        "identity": {
          "graphId": "topic-template"
        },
        "documentation": "ScriptRunner.js runs user script text inside a sandboxed <iframe sandbox=\"allow-scripts\">, compiled via new Function('api', ...), talking to the host over postMessage RPC with a per-run token, a 15s timeout, and a 200-RPC cap. The host side (usePluginRuntime.js) enforces its own mutation budget and wires RPC methods (getNodes, createNode, updateNode, createEdge, deleteNode, applyDeltas, events) to the real GraphCRUD mutation class — scripts genuinely can read and write graph nodes/edges, subject to allowMutations/dryRun toggles on the node. Separately, graphExecutionRuntime.js topologically sorts nodes and routes each one's currently-stored output to downstream nodes by sourcePort/targetPort, emitting a real nodeInput event that node components (ScriptNode, TimerNode) actually listen for and act on.",
        "examples": "The node types found: timer, delay, valueTrigger, api (client-side fetch on trigger), script, event-declaration/event-handler/method/subscription — all real, all wired, all comparable in kind to n8n's Code node and trigger/action nodes."
      }
