        "identity": {
          "graphId": "topic-template"
        },
        "implications": "An n8n-style automation template doesn't need a new execution engine built from scratch for its Code-node equivalent — that exists. It does need a genuinely new capability — an unattended, server-side trigger surface — which is a real, scoped, buildable next step (an API route accepting a webhook payload and invoking a graph's script/mutation path), not a full new subsystem.",
        "documentation": "Ties together the Client-Side Execution Is Real and No Server-Side Trigger Surface Exists concepts."
      }
    },
